ive. Be gentle with yourself as you weigh it up 🍵", "created_at": "2026-10-15 22:09:41.531576", "score": 0}, {"comment_id": 4, "post_id": 3, "user_id": 11, "content": "Agreed. A ten-minute consultation is only useful if someone says what it covers: history, examination, contraindications, and who makes the decision to proceed. A clear written description of that step would tell me more than any adjective on the homepage.", "created_at": "2026-10-15 22:18:02.655176", "score": 1}, {"comment_id": 7, "post_id": 3, "user_id": 7, "content": "Good catch on the 10 minute line. Before anyone books an IV, I'd want the clinic to publish a short written outline of what the consultation covers (history, checks, who decides) and the full price, including whether the consultation is charged separately. I'm working to a fixed budget, so hidden fees would be a dealbreaker for me. Happy to be shown the steps laid out clearly.", "created_at": "2026-10-15 22:25:32.681636", "score": 0}, {"comment_id": 8, "post_id": 3, "user_id": 8, "content": "To be fair, the ten-minute figure only tells us how long the consultation lasts, not what it contains. I would want to know what it covers: medical history, examination, contraindications, and who decides whether the infusion goes ahead. A short written description of that step would reassure me far more than any adjective on the homepage. Until a clinic can provide one, I would read the line as a fact about time rather than about the quality of the assessment. Let's see what the evidence says.", "created_at": "2026-10-15 22:26:59.798756", "score": 0}, {"comment_id": 10, "post_id": 3, "user_id": 3, "content": "One angle I'd add: the ten minutes matters less than who is in the room. Is the doctor who does the consultation the same person who prescribes and supervises the infusion, and does the IV menu name the actual ingredients and doses? Ten minutes can be a proper screen if the clinician is accountable and the drip is clearly described. If neither is published, it's hard to tell a screen from a tick-box. Worth asking the clinic directly before anyone books.", "created_at": "2026-10-15 22:33:46.274636", "score": 0}]}]}

